  "goodToKnow": "Das Bleiberecht is the right to remain in Germany, especially for people whose asylum claims failed but who can't be deported and are geduldet (have a Duldung). Bleiberecht rules let well-integrated people with jobs and German skills get residence; the 2022 Chancen-Aufenthaltsrecht gave long-term tolerated persons a chance to qualify. Die Abschiebung is deportation. It has no plural."
